WEBVTT

00:01.543 --> 00:05.422
Well, I'm 14, so 21 is a geezer, for sure.

00:09.467 --> 00:10.635
Ugh, that sucks!

00:10.719 --> 00:14.097
That's so disgusting!
I could report you for harassment.

00:14.180 --> 00:15.223
<i>What's with this</i>

00:15.306 --> 00:17.392
<i>- entitled germaphobe?
-</i> Like, I seriously

00:17.475 --> 00:18.935
don't want to get dirty. I hate it.

00:19.853 --> 00:22.731
I need to keep clean...

00:25.984 --> 00:27.027
<i>A hidden weapon!</i>

00:29.070 --> 00:30.572
<i>Little punk!</i>

00:35.660 --> 00:36.745
<i>What was that?</i>

00:37.412 --> 00:39.289
<i>How did he know all of my moves?</i>

00:43.460 --> 00:44.586
Sorry, kid.

00:45.879 --> 00:46.921
There's someone

00:48.256 --> 00:50.341
I need to catch up to, fast.

02:22.392 --> 02:26.062
KANAGURI

02:28.898 --> 02:33.111
Young boy. You'd do better if you
took your life, rather than apologize.

02:34.404 --> 02:35.905
<i>I need to get better.</i>

02:36.739 --> 02:38.199
<i>I need to be a worthy partner.</i>

02:38.908 --> 02:40.493
<i>I need to do this myself!</i>

02:41.661 --> 02:44.664
Mr. Sakamoto,
when we take this Transfer Exam,

02:44.747 --> 02:46.708
please promise you won't help me out.

02:48.126 --> 02:49.335
Why not?

02:49.419 --> 02:52.171
I don't want to rely on you, Mr. Sakamoto.

02:52.255 --> 02:54.340
I want to see what I'm really capable of.

02:55.466 --> 02:57.051
Fine, just don't fail.

02:57.135 --> 02:59.888
Of course I won't! Just watch me!

03:00.513 --> 03:02.473
<i>I'll pass, top of the group!</i>

03:05.435 --> 03:08.354
<i>Huh? What's this guy's deal?</i>

03:08.438 --> 03:11.524
<i>He totally figured out all my moves.</i>

03:11.608 --> 03:13.192
<i>Was it just dumb luck?</i>

03:13.276 --> 03:15.361
<i>Of course it was. It had to be.</i>

03:15.445 --> 03:16.696
What's wrong?

03:17.280 --> 03:18.364
Come at me.

03:23.661 --> 03:26.581
<i>Seriously, I can't touch him.
What's happening?</i>

03:28.499 --> 03:32.086
So you're going for counterattacks, huh.
In that case...

03:37.508 --> 03:38.927
Whoa, that was close...

03:41.971 --> 03:44.390
<i>No matter how good his instincts are,</i>

03:44.974 --> 03:47.769
<i>they're useless if I hold him in place.</i>

03:49.479 --> 03:50.980
That's a good idea.

03:52.607 --> 03:54.150
Except I heard everything.

03:58.738 --> 04:01.741
Ouch... You're so annoying.

04:01.824 --> 04:04.661
Whatever. Go ahead and kill me, geezer.

04:05.787 --> 04:07.705
As if I'd kill just for a little exam.

04:08.331 --> 04:10.124
And, didn't you say you were 14?

04:10.208 --> 04:12.168
I'll take a JCC bullet from you,

04:12.794 --> 04:14.420
but I'm not into killing kids.

04:24.097 --> 04:27.433
You're a grown-up,
aren't you supposed to go easy on me?

04:27.517 --> 04:29.894
Who even does that?

04:31.980 --> 04:32.939
You're crying?

04:33.523 --> 04:35.275
Shut up, idiot!

04:35.358 --> 04:37.944
Pay for that weapon you broke, geezer.

04:39.862 --> 04:42.073
<i>- Man, talk about a pain!</i>
- I'm gonna fail!

04:42.156 --> 04:44.450
<i>Are kids this entitled nowadays?</i>

04:45.785 --> 04:48.121
Stop crying! It's not that big of a deal!

04:49.205 --> 04:53.084
You're that talented at just 14!
What do you have to whine about?

04:53.626 --> 04:54.585
Talented?

04:55.086 --> 04:57.880
I mean, sure, everyone says that about me.

04:57.964 --> 04:59.590
<i>I wanna punch this punk.</i>

04:59.674 --> 05:01.384
So, if you fail this exam,

05:01.467 --> 05:03.678
just get your license
through an external exam.

05:03.761 --> 05:07.557
Well, it's not like
I really want a license.

05:07.640 --> 05:10.143
I just want to go to the JCC.

05:12.061 --> 05:15.690
I gotta make lots of connections there,
you know,

05:16.649 --> 05:18.026
if I want to join The Order.

05:19.360 --> 05:21.529
The Order? How do you know about--

05:23.197 --> 05:25.533
The moment I've been waiting for!

05:28.244 --> 05:30.371
I call it the "hyena attack."

05:30.455 --> 05:31.706
Die, idiots!

05:36.878 --> 05:39.380
If you want to join The Order,

05:40.506 --> 05:43.301
what you really need isn't connections.

05:43.384 --> 05:44.218
What?

05:46.471 --> 05:48.598
<i>What you need in that world is...</i>

05:50.141 --> 05:52.268
<i>the ultimate set of skills. That's all.</i>

05:53.603 --> 05:56.439
And you better bet I'll be in there, too.

05:59.067 --> 06:00.401
Who are you?

06:01.736 --> 06:02.612
Here.

06:04.572 --> 06:06.074
If you've got one bullet,

06:06.157 --> 06:08.034
you'll at least pass the first stage.

06:08.117 --> 06:09.285
See ya.

06:12.580 --> 06:14.207
Uh, hey,

06:14.290 --> 06:15.708
wait a second.

06:16.417 --> 06:18.252
No need to thank me.

06:18.336 --> 06:21.839
This one's got blood on it,
and it's disgusting. Trade me.

06:21.923 --> 06:24.425
You'd better do something
about your personality!

06:24.509 --> 06:27.553
Come on, I'm the one who
earned the bullets to begin with.

06:27.637 --> 06:28.846
Ugh, fine!

06:28.930 --> 06:30.556
Here. You happy?

06:30.640 --> 06:31.933
SHIN: 1 BULLET
MAFUYU: 2 BULLETS

06:44.821 --> 06:47.865
<i>This isn't good. It's been a while
since the exam began,</i>

06:47.949 --> 06:51.202
<i>and I still don't have a single bullet.
I'm gonna fail the exam...</i>

06:51.702 --> 06:52.537
Hmm?

06:53.913 --> 06:56.541
Who taught you how to handle firearms?

06:58.459 --> 07:00.044
Sorry! I'm so sorry!

07:00.128 --> 07:02.171
I'm terrible with guns.

07:02.255 --> 07:05.133
All I've had was
a relative who showed me a little bit.

07:05.216 --> 07:06.134
Hand me that.

07:07.301 --> 07:08.678
Uh, sure.

07:08.761 --> 07:11.806
It's more stable
if you tilt it forward when shooting.

07:11.889 --> 07:13.141
Arch your back like this.

07:13.641 --> 07:17.311
Hold it securely against your shoulder
to get a straight trajectory.

07:19.689 --> 07:21.399
Shit. How dare you!

07:21.482 --> 07:24.402
The wrist against the handguard
stays relaxed.

07:24.485 --> 07:27.405
That's amazing.
You're so good at explaining it.

07:27.488 --> 07:29.657
I can't believe you're a rookie like me.

07:31.117 --> 07:34.704
<i>I once tutored someone your age.</i>

07:34.787 --> 07:36.330
<i>Wow!</i>

07:36.914 --> 07:39.584
Oh, by the way, I forgot to ask your name.

07:39.667 --> 07:41.252
I'm Sa--

07:41.335 --> 07:42.336
Taro.

07:42.879 --> 07:44.130
I'm Akira.

07:44.630 --> 07:46.340
Nice to meet you, Mr. Taro!

07:51.679 --> 07:53.806
Who fired those shots?

07:54.474 --> 07:55.975
They've got a steady hand!

07:57.351 --> 07:59.061
Damn it. How dare he...

08:01.564 --> 08:04.233
- I'll get you!
- You slithery prick!

08:04.317 --> 08:08.237
Yes, wonderful!
Great facial expressions, everyone!

08:10.281 --> 08:11.616
Scene, hit man exam.

08:12.575 --> 08:15.536
Candidates hone their skills
with their lives at stake.

08:15.620 --> 08:18.623
Give me more excitement
and more gritty realism!

08:19.123 --> 08:21.501
To captivate the audience,

08:21.584 --> 08:23.336
we need just a dash of hope...

08:23.878 --> 08:25.546
It's mine!

08:26.088 --> 08:26.923
Right there!

08:28.549 --> 08:30.426
Cut!

08:35.973 --> 08:36.974
...and despair!

08:37.517 --> 08:39.018
Like in the movie <i>Funny Games.</i>

08:40.436 --> 08:43.731
I'm so glad I applied for this
part-time gig as an examiner.

08:44.357 --> 08:46.025
I think I'll get some great shots.

08:47.109 --> 08:48.945
KANAGURI
EXAMINER - DIRECTOR - ORDER MEMBER

08:59.747 --> 09:02.041
<i>Candidates, may I have your attention.</i>

09:02.625 --> 09:07.004
<i>Out of the 360 candidates,
297 are out of commission.</i>

09:07.588 --> 09:09.924
<i>There are 63 candidates
remaining in the exam.</i>

09:10.007 --> 09:12.385
We'll be landing in roughly 30 minutes.

09:12.885 --> 09:15.137
We hope you enjoy
the remainder of your flight.

09:18.140 --> 09:20.685
Any thoughts on this year's Transfer Exam?

09:20.768 --> 09:23.145
Thoughts? Are you kidding?

09:23.229 --> 09:26.566
Half of the examiners are out.
That's never happened before.

09:27.108 --> 09:30.570
Well, it's not like that matters
to us pilots, anyway.

09:33.823 --> 09:35.283
Stop following me!

09:35.366 --> 09:39.870
Hey Shin, why are you
even taking this exam?

09:40.371 --> 09:41.872
That's none of your business.

09:42.665 --> 09:43.499
Aw, c'mon.

09:43.583 --> 09:45.585
Please? Just tell me.

09:45.668 --> 09:46.752
- Young boys.
- Shin.

09:46.836 --> 09:49.046
- Could they be rookies?
- Stop nagging me!

09:49.130 --> 09:50.715
- They're still so young.
- Drop it.

09:50.798 --> 09:52.925
- So why choose this life?
- I told you mine.

09:53.009 --> 09:54.677
You blabbed on without me asking!

09:55.303 --> 09:57.096
I told you to stop following me!

09:57.179 --> 10:00.600
Please? Don't be such a petty geezer.

10:00.683 --> 10:01.726
Hmm?

10:01.809 --> 10:03.394
What'd you call me, you brat!

10:03.477 --> 10:04.645
- Great!
- I am not...

10:04.729 --> 10:06.063
- Now zoom in...
- ...a geezer!

10:06.147 --> 10:07.732
- That's it.
- And I'm not petty!

10:08.316 --> 10:09.984
Hey! I need a smooth shot here!

10:10.568 --> 10:11.694
The dolly's shaking!

10:12.236 --> 10:14.030
And, cut!

10:14.113 --> 10:15.489
You both have a great look!

10:16.365 --> 10:17.283
For your troubles.

10:20.369 --> 10:21.245
An examiner!

10:23.831 --> 10:24.915
Wait.

10:24.999 --> 10:26.208
Could that be...

10:26.959 --> 10:29.003
Kanaguri, the movie director?

10:30.796 --> 10:33.007
You know me, young boy?

10:33.090 --> 10:34.467
What? Who's that?

10:34.550 --> 10:36.886
How could you not know Kanaguri?!

10:36.969 --> 10:38.471
Founder of Murder Films,

10:38.554 --> 10:41.390
director, screenwriter, casting director,
and cameraman!

10:41.474 --> 10:43.184
Thanks to his unique filming method,

10:43.267 --> 10:45.978
his portrayals of hitmen are
authentic yet sensational,

10:46.062 --> 10:48.939
and his works have
a worldwide cult following!

10:49.023 --> 10:52.902
He's <i>the</i> Kanaguri,
pioneer of hit men films!

10:52.985 --> 10:54.111
Hey, calm down.

10:54.195 --> 10:56.822
You're spitting on me. It's disgusting!

10:56.906 --> 11:01.494
So, what are you doing here,
Mr. bigshot film director?

11:01.577 --> 11:04.121
Isn't it obvious?
I'm shooting my next film.

11:04.664 --> 11:06.248
I just happened to have business here.

11:06.916 --> 11:09.627
What? Stop filming me, you creep.

11:09.710 --> 11:10.628
Watch it!

11:10.711 --> 11:12.171
Forget that the cameras are here.

11:12.838 --> 11:14.548
I want to film your authentic selves.

11:15.091 --> 11:16.842
Did you not hear me?

11:16.926 --> 11:18.302
But what's the issue?

11:18.886 --> 11:21.263
Do you understand
you'd be featured in my film?

11:21.889 --> 11:24.308
Ugh, what a piece of work.

11:24.892 --> 11:27.019
Let's go, Shin.

11:27.103 --> 11:29.021
Movies are overrated, anyway.

11:29.105 --> 11:30.523
What? Hey!

11:32.149 --> 11:33.526
What did you just say?

11:33.609 --> 11:36.737
Movies are so long,
and you can't skip through,

11:36.821 --> 11:38.155
and they're loud...

11:38.697 --> 11:40.950
Isn't it better to watch videos online?

11:41.784 --> 11:44.286
I can just Google the synopsis
for any movie I want.

11:44.787 --> 11:46.372
How dare you!

11:46.455 --> 11:47.289
Stop right there.

11:49.875 --> 11:51.961
Anyone who insults the art of film...

11:52.586 --> 11:53.504
deserves to die.

11:55.714 --> 11:56.632
Get back!

12:01.720 --> 12:02.638
<i>He's so fast.</i>

12:03.139 --> 12:04.974
<i>But I can still predict his moves.</i>

12:09.478 --> 12:10.312
<i>Huh?!</i>

12:10.896 --> 12:13.899
<i>The moves I see are pre-determined
subconsciously.</i>

12:13.983 --> 12:16.652
<i>How could he possibly change them?!</i>

12:25.327 --> 12:26.328
Mr. Sakamoto!

12:26.996 --> 12:29.999
Don't pull at the muzzle like that,
Mr. Taro!

12:30.499 --> 12:32.585
We could've shot someone by accident!

12:33.127 --> 12:34.003
Sorry.

12:35.880 --> 12:36.755
You're perfect!

12:37.339 --> 12:39.633
That smooth silhouette of your body,

12:40.176 --> 12:42.720
that soft aura,
seemingly foreign to killing...

12:43.262 --> 12:44.513
A jewel like aesthetic!

12:45.097 --> 12:46.891
I've finally found you!

12:46.974 --> 12:50.019
You are everything that I want
in my main character!

12:50.102 --> 12:51.228
What's up with him?

12:51.854 --> 12:53.606
Does he have a weird fetish?

12:54.106 --> 12:55.274
I've decided.

12:55.357 --> 12:56.609
You're my protagonist.

12:56.692 --> 12:57.526
What?!

13:00.738 --> 13:02.615
The hook is key in filmmaking.

13:03.866 --> 13:05.534
It's got to be flashy and catchy.

13:06.076 --> 13:07.119
Right, yes...

13:07.203 --> 13:08.454
I can see it now...

13:10.414 --> 13:12.291
Got it. Let's do this!

13:13.709 --> 13:14.543
What?

13:22.843 --> 13:25.554
It's time to start shooting!

13:33.229 --> 13:34.605
I'm so sorry!

13:34.688 --> 13:37.525
What's going on? I can't hold myself up...

13:39.193 --> 13:40.110
Oops, sorry.

13:40.194 --> 13:43.155
Hmm, not as dramatic as I thought it'd be.

13:44.031 --> 13:46.116
Boring! Scrap this scene!

13:46.867 --> 13:50.079
This won't draw the audience in.

13:51.288 --> 13:53.749
What the-- What is he trying to do now?

13:56.085 --> 13:57.169
Ready!

14:03.133 --> 14:04.343
Listen up, assassins!

14:07.429 --> 14:10.849
This is... a movie!

14:19.483 --> 14:23.571
Damn it. What are we gonna do?
This will take out all the candidates.

14:23.654 --> 14:24.488
Who's at fault?

14:24.572 --> 14:25.406
USAMI
HEAD EXAMINER

14:25.489 --> 14:26.615
Am I responsible for this?

14:26.699 --> 14:30.995
Thank goodness we brought
parachutes for us examiners.

14:31.078 --> 14:34.915
This is why I was against
hiring that weird film director!

14:34.999 --> 14:36.166
What?

14:36.250 --> 14:38.419
Are you saying I'm responsible for this?

14:39.044 --> 14:42.047
Aw man, will they get mad at me?
This blows.

14:42.590 --> 14:45.676
I wish someone else would
take the blame instead.

14:45.759 --> 14:49.680
Don't worry, Mr. Usami.
I've got a good idea.

14:49.763 --> 14:52.683
We can just say
this whole thing is the second stage.

14:52.766 --> 14:54.435
Ms. Ato, you are a genius!

14:54.935 --> 14:55.769
Going with that.

14:57.980 --> 15:00.316
Err, attention candidates.

15:00.399 --> 15:04.945
We will now be conducting the second round
of the examination, as planned.

15:05.613 --> 15:08.616
To pass, you must be
in possession of one bullet,

15:08.699 --> 15:11.702
and survive the landing. That is all.

15:12.244 --> 15:14.747
<i>What? That wasn't what we discussed.</i>

15:14.830 --> 15:15.664
NORO
EXAMINER

15:15.748 --> 15:18.751
<i>I'm an examiner
but they didn't get me a parachute.</i>

15:19.585 --> 15:21.795
"As planned," my ass!

15:23.213 --> 15:24.548
Damn it!

15:24.632 --> 15:28.052
Why is this year's exam
so different from the others!

15:28.135 --> 15:29.803
Shut up, idiot.

15:30.346 --> 15:32.973
You can survive an airplane crash
without parachutes.

15:33.057 --> 15:36.143
There have been 15 such cases
in the past decade.

15:36.226 --> 15:37.061
Really?

15:38.062 --> 15:40.272
We have enough oxygen to breathe.

15:40.814 --> 15:42.650
And based on our flight path,

15:42.733 --> 15:44.985
we should be near
an altitude of 20,000 feet.

15:45.694 --> 15:49.323
Falling at the average speed of
120 miles per hour,

15:49.907 --> 15:51.825
we should have about two minutes left.

15:52.409 --> 15:56.455
You think you'd fall into the ocean,
but water is hardly compressible.

15:56.538 --> 15:59.667
From this height,
it'd be like hitting concrete.

16:02.836 --> 16:04.755
I'm gonna die!

16:04.838 --> 16:06.382
That sucks!

16:06.465 --> 16:07.466
Stop crying!

16:09.969 --> 16:10.970
Wonderful!

16:11.053 --> 16:13.389
Truly on the verge of life and death!

16:14.014 --> 16:15.432
Absolutely authentic!

16:16.058 --> 16:18.394
Our hero now faces an unexpected calamity!

16:18.978 --> 16:21.021
How will she overcome this crisis?

16:23.565 --> 16:25.317
This is what I'm talkin' about!

16:35.744 --> 16:37.413
Got them back.

16:37.496 --> 16:38.414
I see.

16:38.998 --> 16:41.166
Quite a performance by
our supporting cast.

16:41.250 --> 16:42.626
Mr. Sakamoto!

16:42.710 --> 16:45.671
We should focus on how to land right now,
not him.

16:46.255 --> 16:48.132
Even if we get through this safely,

16:48.215 --> 16:50.759
we'd be disqualified without the bullets.

16:51.385 --> 16:52.219
<i>This guy...</i>

16:52.761 --> 16:55.222
<i>Everyone's panicking, trying to survive,</i>

16:55.305 --> 16:57.641
<i>and he's the only one
thinking beyond that.</i>

16:58.267 --> 16:59.268
Don't worry, Shin.

16:59.935 --> 17:02.855
I brought my apron
in case of emergencies like this.

17:04.064 --> 17:05.399
Of course!

17:05.482 --> 17:07.609
We can make our own parachute!

17:10.487 --> 17:12.281
No, Mr. Sakamoto!

17:12.948 --> 17:15.367
<i>- Mr. Taro isn't giving up hope.</i>
- Mr. Sakamoto!

17:16.076 --> 17:17.077
<i>- Watching him...</i>
- Wait!

17:17.161 --> 17:18.829
<i>...gives me courage!</i>

17:18.912 --> 17:21.123
<i>I'm not going to give up, either.</i>

17:21.749 --> 17:24.251
<i>I just have to do what I can,
and give it all I've got.</i>

17:24.793 --> 17:27.087
<i>So, what can I do?</i>

17:27.171 --> 17:30.257
<i>I can do laundry, clean...</i>

17:32.259 --> 17:34.219
<i>I'm good with household chores, but...</i>

17:37.431 --> 17:41.560
Akira! Would you mind
sewing this button on for me?

17:41.643 --> 17:43.353
Again?!

17:43.437 --> 17:46.190
You'll be an amazing homemaker, Akira!

17:46.774 --> 17:48.525
Don't become an assassin, okay?

17:51.195 --> 17:52.321
<i>I've gotta do it.</i>

17:54.448 --> 17:57.409
Everybody! Please take your clothes off!

17:58.702 --> 18:01.080
I don't have time to explain.

18:01.163 --> 18:02.122
Just give me--

18:02.790 --> 18:03.749
All yours.

18:03.832 --> 18:04.708
I'm in!

18:04.792 --> 18:07.711
Why are we doing this? It's so chilly.

18:07.795 --> 18:08.712
Hurry up!

18:09.463 --> 18:11.048
- My clothes.
- Keep the pants!

18:11.131 --> 18:12.216
Do we even know you?!

18:12.299 --> 18:14.968
You see, sewing happens to be...

18:15.803 --> 18:16.762
my thing!

18:37.074 --> 18:37.991
It's done!

18:43.330 --> 18:46.041
It's definitely slowing us down,
but not enough!

18:46.125 --> 18:48.669
Everybody, please hold on at the edges!

18:50.129 --> 18:51.088
We're getting close!

18:51.171 --> 18:53.924
We got no choice!
Make sure you go in feet first!

19:01.890 --> 19:02.724
<i>Yes!</i>

19:03.267 --> 19:04.309
<i>I survived!</i>

19:05.435 --> 19:06.270
<i>But...</i>

19:06.353 --> 19:09.606
<i>Oh no... I can't swim!</i>

19:10.149 --> 19:12.276
<i>I tried so hard to get here...</i>

19:26.957 --> 19:28.959
I wanna go home...

19:31.920 --> 19:34.006
Man, I thought we were gonna die.

19:34.089 --> 19:37.134
My shoes are all soggy. This sucks!

19:38.051 --> 19:41.054
Let's kill that film director.

19:41.138 --> 19:43.974
Yeah. I'm never watching
another movie he makes.

19:50.272 --> 19:51.523
Why don't you take that?

19:53.275 --> 19:54.610
But it's not mine.

19:55.611 --> 19:59.489
This time, you definitely
earned that bullet yourself.

20:01.783 --> 20:02.784
I guess so!

20:02.868 --> 20:04.203
Thank you.

20:04.286 --> 20:06.121
I'll be able to pass the second stage!

20:06.663 --> 20:08.165
I've got one, too.

20:08.790 --> 20:09.833
I don't have any...

20:10.709 --> 20:12.294
But I'm grateful to be alive!

20:18.091 --> 20:20.010
What's wrong, Mr. Sakamoto?

20:20.677 --> 20:21.720
<i>These stitches...</i>

20:22.763 --> 20:25.933
<i>The needlework is incredibly meticulous.</i>

20:26.850 --> 20:28.685
<i>Not to mention how she sewed all this,</i>

20:29.311 --> 20:30.479
<i>while falling, at such speed...</i>

20:32.189 --> 20:33.482
<i>Who on earth is she?</i>

20:40.280 --> 20:42.824
What? Oh my god, the airplane crashed!

20:43.367 --> 20:46.078
If anyone survived that,
they're a heck of a warrior!

20:47.079 --> 20:48.455
I can't wait!

22:21.340 --> 22:22.341
LUNCH TIME

22:22.424 --> 22:25.010
RAMEN

22:25.093 --> 22:27.846
All I've had are pork buns these days.

22:27.929 --> 22:30.474
I wish I could eat ramen once in a while.

22:34.144 --> 22:35.228
Piisuke?

22:35.312 --> 22:37.230
ONE HOUR LATER

22:38.523 --> 22:40.859
Piisuke, you're back.

22:43.320 --> 22:45.072
What's that rock you've got?

22:46.823 --> 22:48.116
PAWN SHOP - TRADE-INS

22:48.200 --> 22:49.034
What?!

22:49.117 --> 22:51.787
You'll buy that for 1,000 yen? Seriously?

22:52.913 --> 22:55.999
It really is just a random rock,

22:56.083 --> 22:57.542
but it's kinda pretty, so yeah.

22:59.503 --> 23:03.048
This is awesome!
We can finally get some ramen!

23:05.926 --> 23:08.345
STEAMED PORK BUN
250 YEN PER PIECE

23:13.308 --> 23:16.186
It's unusual for you to treat us.

23:16.269 --> 23:17.104
<i>Tasty.</i>

23:20.398 --> 23:23.735
Everything tastes better
when we eat together!

23:23.819 --> 23:25.946
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
